    {
      "id": "QCP-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-quantum-column-alternation",
      "title": "Successive unit shifts make the ordered quantum minor alternating in columns",
      "hypotheses": "An associative unital complex algebra of operators and generators Eab satisfying the gl(m) matrix-unit commutators. In the application they act on a common smooth-vector space.",
      "statement": "For the row-alternated, column-ordered minor with parameters u,u−1,…, the sign changes under each adjacent column interchange. A repeated column makes the minor zero.",
      "definitions": [
        "No factor is commuted past a prefix or suffix. For the two varied positions the sum of four ordered products equals (x−y−1)L, where L is the displayed linear combination of matrix units."
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
