    {
      "id": "QCP-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-quantum-projector-specialization",
      "title": "At a simple root the comatrix extracts a single shifted eigensummand",
      "hypotheses": "On smooth vectors, the Capelli determinant acts by ∏j(u+tj), where tj=λj−N/2. The signed tensor decomposes into distinct eigensummands as in STM-01.",
      "statement": "At −ts the comatrix divided by ∏j≠s(tj−ts) is the s-projector. The scalar denominator is nonzero and its reciprocal has absolute value ≤1 for the regular integral parameter differences.",
      "definitions": [
        "C(u) has degree at most N; cancellation away from the one forbidden point gives equality there by polynomial interpolation.",
        "In the two-dimensional defining representation the determinant is u²−1 and C(−1)=−E on the four-dimensional tensor, giving the spectral projector E/2."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "QCP-02",
        "STM-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-quantum-cofactor-projector"
      ],
